PHASE 6 — FILE READING

1. Full file reading
   → Can we read an entire text file correctly?

2. Line-range reading
   → Can we request only specific lines, e.g. 2–4?

3. Line numbers
   → Does the returned content include line numbers so the model
     can refer to exact code locations later?

4. Missing-file handling
   → What happens when the requested file doesn't exist?

5. Directory validation
   → What happens if the agent tries to read a directory
     instead of a file?

6. Path-traversal protection
   → Can the agent be prevented from reading files outside
     the repository?
     
     Example:
       ../secret.txt  → BLOCKED

7. Invalid line-range handling
   → Does the tool reject invalid requests such as line 0?

8. File-size protection
   → Does the tool prevent excessively large files from being
     loaded into the model context?

9. Binary-file protection
   → Does the tool avoid treating images/executables/etc.
     as normal text?

10. Structured result
    → Does the function return a ToolResult that the agent can
      understand instead of crashing?